{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"5dd3d88f057860a69382644d288536e4223fbbf7be6a5a05f31e3a1774c74380","digest":{"component_or_area":"nginx edge routing for MCP OAuth metadata","key_entities":["infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template","/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp","location = /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp","proxy_pass http://rebar_mcp","tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py","location /.well-known/acme-challenge/","resource_metadata"],"problem_keywords":["oauth metadata discovery","well-known endpoint","nginx routing","404 not found","rfc 9728"],"propositions":["The MCP endpoint's 401 challenge advertises an OAuth metadata URL that returns 404 at the edge because nginx has no location block routing it","The nginx config declares routes for /mcp and /.well-known/acme-challenge/ but not for /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp, so requests fall through to the Gerrit backend","The MCP application already serves 200 responses for /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp on direct connection, confirming the fix requires only an nginx routing rule","An exact-match location block must be added to infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template proxying to the rebar_mcp upstream without modifying the URI path, before the catch-all location / block"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787950641222651155,"uuid":"a45e37ec-421c-4dcf-adee-abfb63123bfe"}